message.content:
This looks like a CBP ruling on iron sign brackets. Candidates are 7326.90 (other articles of iron or steel) and 8302.50 (hat racks, hat-pegs, brackets and similar fixtures, base metal). Heading 8302 covers mounting fittings suitable for buildings, and 8302.42 covers other mountings suitable for furniture. 8302.50 is for hat racks, hat-pegs, brackets and similar fixtures. Sign brackets fixed to a wall would be "brackets and similar fixtures", so 8302.50.00 fits. The statistical suffix for 8302.50.00 is 8302.50.0000, and I recall the subheading has no further breakdown.

The material is a decorative iron bracket with a cast iron tip, and some rulings put such items in 7326.90.8688 as other articles of iron or steel. Note 2 to Section XV defines "parts of general use" as including articles of heading 8302, so the bracket would fall in 8302 if it is a bracket of that type. Heading 8302 covers base metal mountings, fittings and similar articles suitable for buildings. The bracket is a wall bracket for supporting a sign, so 8302.50.0000 is the best fit.

{"hts_code": "8302.50.0000", "reason": "Wall-mounted iron brackets that project from a surface to support a hanging sign are base-metal brackets and similar fixtures of heading 8302, classified in subheading 8302.50."}
